======================================================================================================================
L61 -- THE THREE PERMITTED BRANCHES: >=3 modes, two metrics, non-minimal coupling
======================================================================================================================
The foliation theorem (L31 53/53, L39 40/40, PAPER9) closes ONE corner and names three it does not.
This lane searches the three, and asks first whether the 'excess spent once' theorem follows them there.
a0 footings: canonical 9.3619e-11 m/s^2,  alt 1.1279e-10 m/s^2   (both carried throughout)

======================================================================================================================
PART A -- CONTROLS.  The gate machinery is calibrated against a known object before anything rests on it.
======================================================================================================================

A.1  The four mode-counting controls.  Dirac's formula, one line, applied to four theories whose
     answers are published:   N_phys = (P - 2F - S) / 2,  P = phase-space dimension per space point,
     F = number of first-class constraints, S = number of second-class constraints.

      theory                                 phase space                         F  S    N  published
      general relativity                     gamma_ij (6) -> P = 12              4  0    2          2
          4 first class = Hamiltonian + 3 momentum constraints (the diffeomorphisms)
      GR + one minimally coupled scalar      gamma_ij (6) + phi (1) -> P = 14    4  0    3          3
          the scalar adds no constraint: 2 tensor + 1 scalar
      khronometric (non-projectable Horava)  gamma_ij (6) + khronon T (1) -> P = 14  4  0    3          3
          gauge = foliation-preserving diffeos: 3 spatial + 1 time reparametrisation t -> f(t)
      Einstein-aether                        gamma_ij (6) + u^mu (4) minus the unit constraint (1) -> P = 18  4  0    5          5
          2 tensor + 2 vector + 1 scalar (Jacobson-Mattingly)
