  [PASS] E1b the SLIP repaired has unit magnitude in units of the tilt created: |d(Phi - Psi)| / |tilt| = 1 in BOTH chassis, so a repair of size X costs a cone tilt of size X and there is no lever ratio to exploit   (spacelike 1, timelike 1)
  [PASS] E1c the CONFORMAL factor A alone moves neither: with B = 0 both the tilt and both potential shifts vanish for every A, which is A8 again -- the conformal lever cannot lens and the disformal lever cannot be had without the tilt   (A is pure gauge for light bending; only B moves anything)

