E.6  sf29's two kills, and whether they are the SAME physics as the GW identity.

     (a) SIGN.  The screening boundary condition belongs at the NEWTONIAN end, which for MOND is HIGH
         acceleration, i.e. SMALL r.  With beta = 0 there, integrating outward gives beta < 0 through
         the MOND regime, so the matter cone ratio (v_matter/v_photon)^2 = 1 - beta EXCEEDS 1.
         That is superluminal matter, and it is the SAME quantity as E1's tilt with the opposite sign.
      sf29 reports beta = -1.15 v_c^2 at x = 1 and -4.19 v_c^2 at x = 0.1; at v_c = 150 km/s that is
        cone ratio (v_matter/v_photon)^2 = 1 - beta = 1.000000288, i.e. superluminal by 2.88e-07
        E1's identity says the same number is the lensing shift; sf29 and LOCAL_NO_GO 3.2 AGREE.
  [PASS] E6  sf29's superluminality and the GW-speed identity are the SAME quantity seen from two sides, so there was never a contradiction to adjudicate -- only a stale prose paragraph   ((v_m/v_gamma)^2 - 1 = -beta = 2.879e-07 = the tilt)

     (b) THE THEOREM, which is stronger than the sign.  The no-slip condition gives beta' = -2 Delta
         with Delta = the anomalous acceleration > 0, so beta is STRICTLY MONOTONE in r.  Screening
         requires beta = 0 in BOTH Newtonian regimes -- the high-acceleration interior AND the
         external-field-dominated far exterior.  A strictly monotone function cannot vanish at both.
         Reproduced here with the DEPOSITED theory's own kernel rather than sf29's chassis kernel.

